<title>SPAIN: Lisbon air cargo rose 1.7 percent in August.</title>
<headline>Lisbon air cargo rose 1.7 percent in August.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo traffic at Lisbon airport rose 1.7 percent in August to 7,800 tonnes and 64,135 tonnes in the first eight months, a decrease of 0.9 percent on last year, the Portuguese airport authority, ANA said.</p>
<p>Traffic at Porto, the country's second busiest airport, was 1.4 percent higher this year than in August 1995 taking the monthly total to 1,767 tonnes. In the year to date, volumes increased by 2.9 percent to 16,234 tonnes.</p>
<p>-Air Cargo Newsroom tel:+44 171 542 7706 fax:+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
